# Project map (cursor-esp32 workspace)

| Repo | What it is |
|------|------------|
| **lego-rover-esp32** | LEGO rover firmware — LilyGO T-Display S3, motors, IMU, sonar pan, IR, display, OTA |
| **lego-rover-ros2** | Fleet brain on **dockerhost** (Docker/ROS 2 Jazzy) — wander, logging, coordination. **No Pi.** |
| **c3-mini-bot** | Small ESP32-C3 swarm bots — thin clients, namespaced topics, fleet via dockerhost |
| **yoRadio-fusion-pros3** | yoRadio fork — Fusion Pro S3 internet radio, display, MQTT, NeoStatus |
| **BT-A2DP-Source-HiGrow** | Bluetooth A2DP audio source |
| **GIFPlayer** | GIF playback on ESP display |
| **GoL** | Game of Life (display toy) |
| **Magic-8-Ball** / **Magic-GIF-Ball** | Magic 8 ball variants |
| **NFCNoisy** | NFC-triggered noise toy |
| **lego-roverquest** | Rover-related experiment/quest code |

## Fleet architecture (long-term goal)

- **dockerhost** = brain (ROS 2 Jazzy + micro-ROS agent UDP **8888**).
- Each bot = **thin ESP client** (motors/servos, sensors, local safety, WiFi micro-ROS).
- **bot0** = LEGO rover (`/rover/…`), **bot1+** = c3-minis (`/bot1/…`, unique `BOT_NAMESPACE`).
- Future: **IR pulse patterns** (not 38 kHz TSOP) for bot-to-bot cues.
- Rover agent IP: check `platformio_private.ini` / env flags (e.g. `192.168.2.31`).

